        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c22" value="&lt;b&gt;1.&lt;/b&gt; The client connects to the server over HTTPS.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;2.&lt;/b&gt; Traffic Mirroring copies the packets from the client ENI that match the filter.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;3.&lt;/b&gt; The copies reach the mirror target as VXLAN on UDP 4789, and tcpdump writes them to a capture file.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;4.&lt;/b&gt; The analyst copies the capture file to a workstation and opens it in Wireshark.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;5.&lt;/b&gt; The plugin sends decoded packet fields to Amazon Bedrock and shows the findings in Wireshark." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#232F3E;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="650" width="780" height="120" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
